<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 29 September, from 61 BCE to 1938.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pompey" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">61 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,086 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pompey celebrates his third triumph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> the Great celebrated his third triumph, for his victories over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> and the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridatic-wars">Mithridatic Wars</a>, on his 45th birthday. The settlement of 63 BCE had seen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> annex Pontus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph">Roman triumph</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/855">855 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,171 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Benedict III is restored by a popular uprising</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-of-italy">Louis II of Italy</a>, Carolingian emperor, tried to replace him with his own favoured candidate, Benedict III was restored to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> by a popular uprising. He reigned as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> until his death in April 858.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-of-italy">Louis II of Italy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1227">1227 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">799 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Gregory IX excommunicates Emperor Frederick II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gregory IX excommunicated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> for again delaying his promised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>. Frederick went anyway, regaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> by treaty in 1229 and crowning himself in the Holy Sepulchre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1267">1267 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">759 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry III recognises Llywelyn ap Gruffudd as Prince of Wales</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-montgomery">Treaty of Montgomery</a>, Henry III recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, with overlordship of the other Welsh lords, in return for homage and a large payment. Disputes over these led to Edward I's invasion of 1277.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-montgomery">Treaty of Montgomery</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1364">1364 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">662 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anglo-Breton forces win the Battle of Auray</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Auray, Anglo-Breton forces defeated the Franco-Breton army in the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-breton-succession">War of the Breton Succession</a>, the struggle between the counts of Blois and the Montforts for the Duchy of Brittany. The war ended the following April.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1758">1758 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">268 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Horatio Nelson is born in Norfolk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> was born at Burnham Thorpe, the son of a rector. He won the battles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> and died at his greatest victory, Trafalgar, in 1805.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1829">1829 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">197 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">London's Metropolitan Police go on patrol for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Constables of Robert Peel's new Metropolitan Police began patrolling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. Nicknamed 'Bobbies' or 'Peelers', they set a model of uniformed, civilian policing by consent.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1938">1938 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Munich conference hands the Sudetenland to Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chamberlain, Daladier, Hitler and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> agreed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> must cede the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudetenland">Sudetenland</a>; the deal was signed after midnight. Czechoslovakia was not consulted.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a></div></div></li></ol>
